# This machine's settings. Copy to host.env (git ignores it) and fill in.
# hostctl (which passes it on to what it runs), the systemd units (EnvironmentFile=) and the site builds
# all read it, so keep to KEY=value lines: no quotes, no spaces around =, no $.

# The name this machine is reached by over HTTPS, with a certificate valid for it. The machine
# routes the apps' ports on it to their servers on 127.0.0.1 (tailscale serve, Caddy, …;
# `uv run hostctl routes` lists and checks them), the service containers reach AnythingLLM
# and SearXNG by it, and every link the setup hands out uses it.
PUBLIC_HOST=machine.example.net

# AnythingLLM's storage directory on the host; its container mounts it at /app/server/storage.
ANYTHINGLLM_STORAGE=/srv/anythingllm/storage

# Optional. The ntfy server in the Nilson relay's NTFY_URL, which the egress proxy lets the
# relay's container reach (packages/egress, egress.toml). Unset, it is ntfy.sh.
# NTFY_HOST=ntfy.sh

# Optional. The user's time zone (an IANA name): agents-runner reads one-off jobs' times
# (remind-once) in it and lists scheduled jobs' times in it, while AnythingLLM's cron stays
# UTC. Unset, it is Europe/Stockholm.
# USER_TIMEZONE=Europe/Stockholm
